# Testing standards

Two layers. Both are offline. Neither checks a real PDE workbook into git.

## Parser tests (`pytest`, `tests/`)

Build a tiny xlsx/pdf fixture in the test. Pin the cases that corrupt silently:

- AUN stays nine-digit text (`101260303.0` must not become a float/scientific string).
- `school_year` comes from the catalog fixture, not the sheet title.
- Zeros kept; absent columns produce no row; junk headers are rejected.
- Split rates / multi-county / stacked sheets behave as designed.
- `document_id` is present on fact rows.

Run at least the touched files: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_refine.py tests/test_publish.py -q`.

## Rebuild checks (`python -m pa_edu.check`)

Needs local `data/raw` + `data/refined`. A year moves `review` → `stable` only after these pass for that file.

| Kind | Intent |
| --- | --- |
| Identity | Every fact `aun` ∈ `lea`; every `document_id` has a URL |
| Grain | No duplicate natural keys |
| Cell round-trip | Listed cells in `sources/checks.toml` re-read from the workbook equal parquet |
| Published totals / rollups | Do not sum parent+child or major+component objects |

When adding a source, add a `[[…_cell]]` (or equivalent) that re-opens the raw file independently of the parser output. That is the citation test.
